{"version":1,"reference":{"kind":"artifact_content","namespace":"#1113","artifact_type":"_dh-work-item-head-v1","name":"head"},"owner_reference":"#1113","content":"{\"version\":1,\"issue_reference\":\"#1113\",\"parent_revision\":\"f93567b476f782bbf3945bc6c30563cc0af671b7c140e724697cf8f2d4b59739\",\"root_revision\":\"f93567b476f782bbf3945bc6c30563cc0af671b7c140e724697cf8f2d4b59739\",\"body\":\"<!-- backlog-metadata:\\npriority: P1\\ntype: Chore\\nstatus: open\\nadded: 2026-08-12\\n-->\\n\\n## Description\\n\\nAdd a validation check that cross-references every agent name referenced in skill files, Python functions (build_quality_gate_plan, build_proportional_quality_gate_plan), and YAML task plans against the set of actually registered subagent types. The gap was discovered when complete-implementation QG dispatch silently used the wrong agent (code-review instead of code-reviewer) because the dh plugin had an agents override in plugin.json that made 15 of 16 agents invisible.\\n\\nRoot cause fixed separately (removed agents key from development-harness plugin.json). This item tracks the systemic prevention: a check or pre-commit hook that detects agent name drift before it causes silent failures.\\n\\n**Research first**: Determine whether this is best implemented as:\\n- A skilllint rule that scans agent: fields in YAML task files and skill files\\n- A pre-commit hook that greps for agent name references and validates against plugin manifests\\n- A one-off audit script run manually before releases\\n\\n**Suggested location**: Either `.claude/rules/` (documentation of convention) + a script in `scripts/` (validator), or extend `skilllint` with a new rule.\\n\\n## Groomed (2026-04-02)\\n\\n### Priority\\n\\n7/10 \u2014 Silent dispatch failures are high-severity but the root cause (plugin.json agents override) has been fixed. Remaining risk is future drift; audit provides systemic prevention.\\n\\n### Impact\\n\\n- Blocks: complete-implementation quality gate dispatch when agent names drift from registered inventory\\n- Bottleneck: any QG phase that dispatches to a non-existent agent silently routes to wrong agent or fails without a clear error message\\n\\n### Benefits\\n\\n- Prevents future recurrence of the code-reviewer/code-review silent failure that caused complete-implementation to dispatch incorrectly\\n- Makes agent name references auditable at commit time rather than at runtime\\n- Surfaces cross-plugin dependencies explicitly (code-reviewer lives in python3-development/python-engineering, not dh)\\n\\n### Expected Behavior\\n\\nWhen any agent name referenced in `build_quality_gate_plan`, `build_proportional_quality_gate_plan`, YAML task files, or skill files does not match a registered agent in any installed plugin's agent inventory, the validator reports the unknown name and exits non-zero. All valid names pass silently.\\n\\n### Desired Structure\\n\\nA validator that:\\n- Reads all agent names emitted by `_PHASE_DEFINITIONS` and `_PROPORTIONAL_PHASE_DEFINITIONS` in `quality_gates.py`\\n- Reads the registered agent inventory from all `plugin.json` files (auto-discovered via `agents/` directories since no `agents` key overrides are present)\\n- Reports any names present in the former but absent in the latter\\n\\nThe validator may also scan YAML task files and skill markdown files for `agent:` fields.\\n\\nDelivery options (from item description):\\n1. A script in `scripts/` (standalone, manually runnable)\\n2. A pre-commit hook entry in `.pre-commit-config.yaml`\\n3. A new skilllint rule\\n\\nNote: Option 3 requires extending the external `skilllint` tool \u2014 highest effort, highest reuse.\\n\\n### Acceptance Criteria\\n\\n1. Running the validator against the current codebase reports `code-reviewer` as an agent name referenced in `quality_gates.py` that is not registered in the `dh` plugin's own agent inventory\\n2. The validator exits 0 when all referenced agent names resolve to at least one registered agent across installed plugins\\n3. The validator exits non-zero and prints the unresolved names when any referenced name has no match\\n4. If implemented as a pre-commit hook: the hook runs on changes to `quality_gates.py`, YAML task plan files, and agent `.md` files\\n5. The validator's own test (or manual verification run) is documented in the item or a script comment\\n\\n### Resources\\n\\n| Type | Item |\\n|------|------|\\n| Prior work | plugins/development-harness/sam_schema/core/quality_gates.py \u2014 contains `_PHASE_DEFINITIONS` and `_PROPORTIONAL_PHASE_DEFINITIONS` with hardcoded agent names |\\n| Prior work | plugins/development-harness/.claude-plugin/plugin.json \u2014 no `agents` key; auto-discovery applies |\\n| Prior work | plugins/development-harness/agents/ \u2014 15 registered agents (code-reviewer is absent) |\\n| Prior work | plugins/python3-development/agents/code-reviewer.md \u2014 code-reviewer lives here |\\n| Prior work | plugins/python-engineering/agents/code-reviewer.md \u2014 and here |\\n| Prior work | .pre-commit-config.yaml \u2014 existing hook patterns to follow for new pre-commit hook |\\n| Prior work | plugins/plugin-creator/scripts/plugin_validator.py \u2014 existing plugin validation script (reference for approach) |\\n\\n### Dependencies\\n\\n- Depends on: None \u2014 root cause fix (removal of `agents` key from plugin.json) is already done\\n- Blocks: None identified\\n\\n### Effort\\n\\nSmall (script + hook) to Medium (skilllint rule) \u2014 the data gathering is straightforward (read Python dicts, glob agent files); the complexity is in multi-plugin resolution and deciding what counts as a valid cross-plugin reference.\\n\\n### Blockers\\n\\n- design decision required: validator scope (dh-only vs cross-plugin), delivery mechanism (script vs hook vs skilllint rule), and whether to treat cross-plugin agent references as errors or warnings. `code-reviewer` is intentionally provided by language plugins \u2014 the validator must handle multi-plugin resolution, not just single-plugin lookup.\\n\\n## Story\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\nAs a **maintainer of the project infrastructure**, I want to **agent name reference audit: validate build_quality_gate_plan agent names against registered inventory** so that **the project infrastructure stays healthy**.\\n</div>\\n\\n## Acceptance Criteria\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\n- [ ] Work matches description\\n- [ ] Plan or implementation complete\\n</div>\\n\\n## Context\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\n- **Source**: Session 2026-03-29 \u2014 complete-implementation QG dispatch failed because build_quality_gate_plan emits agent names (code-reviewer, feature-verifier, etc.) that were not registered due to plugin.json agents override bug; the broader gap is no automated check that cross-references emitted agent names against the registered inventory\\n- **Priority**: P1\\n- **Added**: 2026-03-29\\n- **Research questions**: None\\n</div>\\n\",\"digest\":\"4bddb75d0c5d872364ffbf9838f0190b779e0700941a53219436fec7bf71555e\",\"comment_id\":\"IC_kwDOQGimCs8AAAABPS8Spg\"}"}